Summary — August history correction

What happened

A rate change was entered in September. To apply it across the month, ProcessData was run from September 1.
Running from the first of a month re-triggers the prior month's close. August had already been closed, so the re-close refreshed August's history with current September values — interest, balances, and rate. Fees were not affected.
A safeguard to stop a closed month from being closed again had been identified but was not yet deployed.
The rate change prompted the September 1 run and made the discrepancy visible, but the re-close itself is the cause. QA reproduction is underway to confirm this.

Impact

August history records only. Current September data and all fees are unaffected.

Resolution

Restore August history from the verified August 31 backup, using the process already validated in the earlier recovery, with a before/after review prior to committing.
Deploy the safeguard so a closed month cannot be re-closed, however ProcessData is run.
Confirm whether any August reports or invoices were generated from the affected data, and regenerate them after the restore.

Going forward

Rate changes do not require a run from the first of the month. The next regular ProcessData run applies the new rate to the full month automatically.
